  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Long-term conservation of Yellow-cheeked crested gibbon through direct law enforcement and community engagement in southern Mondulkiri, Cambodia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to have well-managed forest landscape that supports increasing wildlife populations, especially gibbons, and improving livelihoods for the people who currently live there. The following objectives and associated activities will be accomplished: (1) Protect gibbons by maintaining extensive law enforcement activities, by (a) continuing proactive law enforcement activities to protect sensitive gibbon habitat, and (b) refining the use of remote sensing and the SMART (Spatial Monitoring and Reporting Tool) software to inform adaptive management; (2) Expand and strengthen community engagement in, and support of, gibbon conservation, by (a) continued capacity building for tourism development and improved community engagement, and (b) further refinement and implementation of robust monitoring of the gibbon populations in the ecotourism area.</narrative>
  </description>
